    {
     "id": "ba24c709-37b2-4205-8911-7e6362b446a9",
     "prompt": "Simplify fully $\\frac{x^2+5x}{x^2+7x+10}$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{x}{x+2}$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{x}{x+7}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{x+5}{x+2}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{x}{x+5}$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Factorising gives $\\frac{x(x+5)}{(x+5)(x+2)}$. Cancelling the common factor $x+5$ leaves $\\frac{x}{x+2}$."
    },
    {
     "id": "806b96fb-2209-4a5c-b52b-453bc5f3b17a",
     "prompt": "Simplify $\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{3}{x+1}$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{5}{2x+1}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{5x+1}{x(x+1)}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{5x+2}{x(x+1)}$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{5x+2}{2x+1}$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The common denominator is $x(x+1)$. The numerator becomes $2(x+1)+3x=5x+2$, giving $\\frac{5x+2}{x(x+1)}$."
    },
    {
     "id": "a8915ed1-3333-499a-b6b9-03c672fc39fa",
     "prompt": "Simplify fully $\\frac{x^2-4}{x+5}\\div\\frac{x-2}{2x+10}$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$x+2$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$2(x-2)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{x+2}{2}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$2(x+2)$",
       "correct": true
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Rewrite the division as multiplication by the reciprocal. Using $x^2-4=(x-2)(x+2)$ and $2x+10=2(x+5)$ allows the common factors to cancel, leaving $2(x+2)$."
    },
    {
     "id": "8b8921a9-4ebe-4d4a-a837-3393a9b5705e",
     "prompt": "Solve $\\frac{3}{x}=\\frac{2}{x+1}$.",
